   381	
   382	---
   383	
   384	## Rollback strategy
   385	
   386	All changes are scoped to `src/atpath-core.js` and `src/main.js`.
   387	There is no settings migration: new keys default safely if absent
   388	(`Object.assign({}, DEFAULT_SETTINGS, await this.loadData())` already
   389	fills missing keys at load).
   390	
   391	If the fix regresses behavior, revert with one commit:
   392	
   393	```
   394	git revert <fix-commit-sha>
   395	npm run build
   396	```
   397	
   398	The instrumentation (`ATPATH_PERF.*`) added in plan 004 stays in
   399	place — it was harmless (`localStorage`-gated) and remains useful for
   400	post-fix verification.
   401	
   402	---
   403	
   404	## Out of scope (intentionally)
   405	
   406	- **Per-file ref concurrency limiting.** A note with 100 single-file
   407	  `@path` refs would still serialize through `await this.getTokenCount`
   408	  in the status-bar loop. Per the perf dump, this is not currently a
   409	  freeze source: per-file `getTokenCount.encode` is single-digit ms
   410	  for small files, and `maxFileSizeMB` already caps the worst case.
   411	  If a future repro shows this matters, batch them the same way Fix
   412	  A batches folder files.
   413	- **Background warmup of folder counts.** We could pre-walk visible
   414	  folder refs on file open. We don't, because the placeholder UX
   415	  from Fix C is good enough and pre-walking creates work the user
   416	  may never need (e.g. they close the file before the popover opens).
   417	- **Worker-thread tokenization.** `gpt-tokenizer` is synchronous and
   418	  runs on the main thread. Moving it to a worker is a larger change
   419	  with bundler implications; defer until the cap+yield approach is
   420	  proven insufficient.
   421	- **Cap UX in settings tab beyond a number input.** No "preview your
   422	  vault's largest folders" widget. Number input + clear help text is
   423	  enough.
   424	
   425	---
   426	
   427	## Risks
   428	
   429	- **Memo poisoning by sentinel.** If a user raises `maxFolderFiles`
   430	  in settings, the previously-memoized `{overCap}` sentinel for a
   431	  folder would still be served. Mitigation: clear `folderTokenMemo`
   432	  on settings save when either `maxFolderFiles` or `maxFileSizeMB`
   433	  changes. Add to `AtPathSettingTab.display` `onChange` handlers.
   434	- **Sentinel-shape callers.** Six call sites; easy to miss one and
   435	  render `[object Object]`. Mitigation: grep for `getCachedFolderTokens`
   436	  and `getFolderTokens` after the change and visually confirm each
   437	  site handles the union return type. The unit test for the render
   438	  site format guards against a regression here.
   439	- **Batch size too small on small vaults.** A 50-file folder
   440	  encoded in 13 batches of 4 with `setTimeout(0)` between adds maybe
   441	  ~50 ms of scheduling overhead. Acceptable; not worth dynamic
   442	  tuning.
   443	
   444	---
   445	
   446	## Acceptance criteria
   447	
   448	- Opening `STATUS_ai_dev.md` produces an interactive status bar
   449	  within 2 seconds.
   450	- Hovering / pinning the popover does not freeze Obsidian.
   451	- Over-cap folders display `> N files` in inline decorations and in
   452	  the popover.
   453	- In-cap folders eventually display their real number after the
   454	  background walk completes.
   455	- Editor keystroke latency stays under 150 ms.

